{
	"id": "effect-fail",
	"text": "What good is success without the failure of others? Effect.fail creates an effect that will always fail with the given value. Here, we'll give it the string \"too chonky,\" an adjective which entirely bypassed my grandmother's lexicon. Now, boom is an Effect that can never succeed, and always fails with our awful string. If we run it with Effect.runSync, it throws. If we add a delay and run it with Effect.runPromise, we, after two glorious seconds, see our promise rejected.",
